Keep screen capture on DMA-buf instead of the legacy wl_shm path.

xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland exhausts its buffer pool on the wl_shm path and then
stops delivering frames (hyprwm/xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland#180):

  [WARN] [pipewire] Asked for a wl_shm buffer which is legacy.
  [ERR]  [screencopy] tried scheduling on already scheduled cb (type 0)
  [LOG]  [screencopy/pipewire] Out of buffers
  [LOG]  [sc] Retrying screencopy (1/10)

GND ends up on that path because every element between capture and encoder is
system-memory only: intervideosink cannot accept memory:DMABuf, and neither can
videoscale or videoconvert. Measured with capture moved to DMA-buf, the portal's
"Out of buffers" and wl_shm warnings both drop to zero.

Two changes:

  - Drop the intervideosink/intervideosrc bridge and ghost the source pad
    directly. Both halves were created in the same per-media bin, so it
    decoupled nothing. It also actively hid failures: intervideosrc re-sends the
    stale surface frame at 30fps, so when capture stalled the sink showed a
    frozen picture while RTP kept flowing and no error surfaced anywhere. Needed
    in both near-identical implementations -- app/nd-window.c for the GUI and
    stream/nd-stream.c for the daemon.

  - Use vapostproc instead of videoscale + videoconvert. It imports
    memory:DMABuf and scales/converts on the GPU. videoscale/videoconvert remain
    as a fallback where vapostproc is unavailable.

Note vapostproc only advertises DMABuf with drm modifier 0x0100000000000009, so
whether this negotiates depends on what modifier the compositor exports.

Not upstreamed.

